      "end_mono": 357625.7589245,
      "raw_response": " ANSWER: SUPPORTED\n\nThe abstract from the study \"Noninvasive ventilation for treatment of acute respiratory failure in patients undergoing solid organ transplantation: a randomized trial\" suggests that noninvasive positive pressure ventilation (NIV) is associated with a lower rate of endotracheal intubation and lower rates of fatal complications, length of stay in the intensive care unit, and intensive care unit mortality in recipients of solid organ transplantation with acute respiratory failure. This seems to contradict the initial claim that NIV is not predictive of acute respiratory failure after solid organ transplantation.",
